    {
      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.64,
      "end": 2.22,
      "text": "Hey there! How's your day?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.113,
      "end": 14.183,
      "text": "It is, and it's a fun hobby. You can start with a heavy pan on the stove or a cheap popcorn popper."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 17.263,
      "end": 24.993,
      "text": "Really. The hot air keeps the beans moving so they roast evenly. Just do it outside or near an open window, there's a lot of smoke and chaff."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 31.828,
      "end": 40.278,
      "text": "Listen for the first crack, a popping sound like popcorn. Stopping shortly after gives a light roast, and keeping going towards a second crack gets darker."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.422,
      "end": 50.252,
      "text": "It's best to let them rest for a day or two. Fresh roasted beans release a lot of gas, and the flavour settles after a short rest."
    }
  ]
